{
  "version": 1,
  "about": "Bundled font registry. Every font is SIL OFL 1.1 (licence file alongside), fetched from github.com/google/fonts/tree/main/ofl/<dir>. mood: calm | hype | warm | nostalgic | techno | luxury | playful | dark (first = strongest fit). role: display | text | accent. width: condensed | normal | wide | extended | variable. contrast: low | mid | high (stroke contrast). energy: [lo, hi] plan energy the face suits. case: preferred headline case. axes: default variation (OpenType tags) for every use; bold_axes: extra for headline/label roles; vary: axis ranges that animate well (text layer 'vary'). pairs: companion faces, best first. Bundled Google Fonts entries (source = google/fonts dir) are the common set. rarity: 'rare' marks faces from independent libre foundries (Velvetyne, Collletttivo, The League of Moveable Type), not in Google Fonts; pick_fonts prefers them for the display role (absent = common). Rare entries record source (URL), foundry, author and licence_id (all OFL-1.1). shape: puffy | fine | tall | crazy. foil: contrasting display faces to set against it (puffy <-> fine/tall), best first. liked: true marks faces the user picked in review (preferred when choosing). colr: true marks COLRv1 colour fonts; PIL's FreeType lacks COLRv1 paint, so they render as flat monochrome outlines (use where silhouettes are fine). Ultra is Apache-2.0 (licence_id, LICENSE-<Name>.txt); all other entries are OFL 1.1. subset: \"latin\" marks files trimmed to Basic Latin, Latin-1 / Latin Extended-A and general punctuation (CJK glyphs dropped to save size; layout features and variation tables kept).",
  "moods": ["calm", "hype", "warm", "nostalgic", "techno", "luxury", "playful", "dark"],
